    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d975">

                <pb facs="0762" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7415</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Mr. Parker,
                        representing American interests in Mexico</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-16T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1916, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. Your 267, March 13, 8 p.m. Practically all reports from American consular
                    officers in Mexico encouraging. Department does not anticipate that withdrawal
                    will be necessary, but should necessity arise you are instructed to entrust
                    representation American interests, Embassy and consular property to British or
                    French representative.</p>
                <p>Department’s March 11, 11 p.m., and March 14, 8 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d975-f1"/>, should be consulted for your guidance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
